<title>UK: German trade seeks free market grain imports.</title>
<headline>German trade seeks free market grain imports.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders bid for the export of 1,000 tonnes of free market barley at a rebate of 32.00 Ecus a tonne and 1,000 tonnes of free-market wheat at a rebate of 22.00 Ecus a tonne, the state grain intervention board BLE said on Thursday by telephone from Frankfurt.</p>
<p>The bids will be considered at the European Union's weekly cereals management committee meeting.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
